WEBVTT

00:04.540 --> 00:07.750
Based on the number of taps,
it should be coming from this direction.

00:08.250 --> 00:09.250
It's up there!

00:10.960 --> 00:13.250
Something big is headed here...

00:13.960 --> 00:16.500
Is that... a dragon?!

00:16.500 --> 00:18.460
No, it's a wyvern!

00:18.920 --> 00:20.330
It can't be...

00:36.790 --> 00:38.790
<b>Farming Life in Another World</b>

00:38.580 --> 00:46.170
Masshiro hikari no naka me o samashite
hajimatteiku sutoorii

00:46.170 --> 00:52.880
Fumidasu atarashii sekai donna hana o sakaseyou?

00:53.080 --> 01:00.460
Kumori sora datte mizutamari de yogoretatte

01:00.460 --> 01:03.330
Bokura wa susumu

01:03.330 --> 01:10.080
Souzou mo shinai mirai ga matteiru kitto

01:10.380 --> 01:13.960
Deatte deatte tsunagatteku

01:13.960 --> 01:17.250
Waraeba mawari mo egao ni naru

01:17.250 --> 01:21.290
Chiisana tane maite sodateyou

01:21.290 --> 01:25.380
Yagate ookina hana ni naru

01:25.380 --> 01:28.880
Koukai ya shippai wa kate ni shite

01:28.880 --> 01:32.170
Karafuru na shiawase de afureru youni

01:32.170 --> 01:36.380
Bokura te o toriatte wakeatte

02:15.210 --> 02:18.630
I never expected a monster like that
to show up here...

02:18.630 --> 02:20.210
Should I try to drive it away?

02:20.210 --> 02:22.960
No, maybe it'll just ignore us
and pass through here...

02:25.170 --> 02:26.710
Lu, defense!

02:36.170 --> 02:37.710
We need to put out the fires!

02:40.170 --> 02:41.420
This is bad.

02:41.420 --> 02:43.330
Yeah. Should we attack it?

02:43.330 --> 02:45.830
I'm not even sure we can pierce its barrier.

02:45.830 --> 02:48.080
I need to make a decision, and fast.

02:48.380 --> 02:50.330
Should we try to escape into the forest?

02:50.330 --> 02:53.000
No, that won't work.
He can follow us from the sky!

02:53.290 --> 02:56.290
I just need to drive him away... but how?

02:56.580 --> 02:59.750
I can't worry about that now.
I need to do something.

03:00.130 --> 03:01.880
I need to protect everyone!

03:11.710 --> 03:13.710
Is this a spear?

03:13.920 --> 03:15.210
Why?

03:15.540 --> 03:17.750
It doesn't matter. Right now,

03:17.750 --> 03:19.960
I'm going to take this power...

03:21.750 --> 03:22.960
and crush him!

03:33.170 --> 03:34.170
Impossible...

03:53.460 --> 03:56.080
We managed to put out all the fires.

03:56.080 --> 03:59.630
There was some damage to the crop fields,
but all of the buildings are fine.

03:59.630 --> 04:00.540
I see.

04:05.460 --> 04:07.630
It looks like I managed to take it down.

04:08.080 --> 04:10.040
Are there are lot of these creatures?

04:10.040 --> 04:12.710
Well, there are some places where they live...

04:12.710 --> 04:16.420
but running into one of them that's
this large is a very rare occurrence.

04:16.830 --> 04:21.170
Is there any possibility that someone sent
this wyvern here specifically to attack us?

04:21.170 --> 04:23.130
I don't think so.

04:23.130 --> 04:25.670
Even if this wyvern was under
someone's command,

04:25.670 --> 04:30.170
they wouldn't send such a rare and
valuable creature off on its own.

04:30.170 --> 04:32.580
It was most likely
a wild creature acting alone.

04:32.580 --> 04:34.040
I see.

04:34.040 --> 04:36.330
So then, I guess we can safely say

04:36.330 --> 04:38.920
that this was nothing more than
an unfortunate but rare incident.

04:39.830 --> 04:41.000
By the way...

04:41.000 --> 04:42.210
What is it?

04:43.710 --> 04:45.790
Can we eat this thing?

04:47.670 --> 04:50.460
Wyvern meat is said to be a delicacy.

04:50.960 --> 04:52.960
In fact, it's said to be so delicious

04:52.960 --> 04:55.420
that supposedly there was once a king
who sent his army into a den of wyverns

04:55.420 --> 04:58.580
to hunt them and bring them back for
the king to taste and see for himself.

04:58.580 --> 05:02.330
I'm pretty sure that story ended with
them all getting burned to death

05:02.330 --> 05:05.460
and then swallowed whole by the wyverns.

05:06.750 --> 05:08.210
Here's the meat in question.

05:09.000 --> 05:12.000
This is a wyvern round steak,
grilled with spices.

05:13.170 --> 05:16.170
I wrapped the breast meat in leaves
and steamed it.

05:16.920 --> 05:19.920
And for the tail meat, I simmered it
into a stew with vegetables.

05:21.790 --> 05:26.250
I thought it would be really tough,
but this meat is so tender!

05:26.250 --> 05:30.500
And to think, a regular knife
couldn't even pierce its skin.

05:30.500 --> 05:33.750
Thif delicafy if ewy fit as dewifish as if loofs!

05:33.750 --> 05:35.000
I didn't understand any of that.

05:35.000 --> 05:36.380
Mmm... this broth is great.
I faid...<b></b>

05:36.380 --> 05:38.500
Mmm... this broth is great.
Swallow your food first.<b></b>

05:38.500 --> 05:41.750
Every bite I take of this tail meat
has more flavor than the last!

05:44.630 --> 05:47.000
Hey, would you have been able
to block an attack

05:47.000 --> 05:48.830
from that spear like
the one he used back there?

05:48.830 --> 05:50.330
Not a chance.

05:50.330 --> 05:53.210
That attack pierced a
3-layer barrier from a wyvern

05:53.210 --> 05:56.250
and then proceeded to
blow right through its chest.

05:57.170 --> 05:59.580
Maybe it was actually a stroke of luck

05:59.580 --> 06:02.170
that Kuro and the dogs were who
we ran into first when we came here.

06:02.170 --> 06:03.920
Yeah, you're right.

06:04.580 --> 06:05.750
What's wrong?

06:05.750 --> 06:07.250
Did I not get all the bones out?

06:07.250 --> 06:11.420
No, it's just... we think we're blessed to
be able to enjoy our meals in good health.

06:11.420 --> 06:14.170
We were just thanking fate
for smiling upon us.

06:14.170 --> 06:15.420
It's not that big of a deal.

06:16.170 --> 06:17.460
This one's delicious, too!

06:17.460 --> 06:18.330
It really is!

06:23.830 --> 06:27.040
<b>Demonic Kingdom of Galgardo</b>

06:23.830 --> 06:27.040
<b>Demon Lord's Castle</b>

06:24.830 --> 06:27.040
You say a wyvern was felled?!

06:27.170 --> 06:28.460
Enough of these jokes!

06:28.460 --> 06:30.750
No, the report we received is true.

06:30.750 --> 06:32.040
Impossible!

06:32.040 --> 06:36.290
One of those simply drawing near requires
that we mobilize our entire military force!

06:36.290 --> 06:37.500
This is...

06:37.630 --> 06:40.500
He was attacked from the ground
and killed in two hits.

06:37.630 --> 06:40.130
<b>One of the demon lord's four great generals</b>

06:37.630 --> 06:40.130
<b>Beezel</b>

06:40.130 --> 06:41.630
<b>One of the demon lord's four great generals</b>

06:40.130 --> 06:41.630
<b>Randan</b>

06:40.500 --> 06:41.630
That's absurd!

06:41.630 --> 06:43.170
Enough of these jokes!

06:41.630 --> 06:44.330
<b>One of the demon lord's four great generals</b>

06:41.630 --> 06:44.330
<b>Grattz</b>

06:43.170 --> 06:44.330
It's true.

06:44.670 --> 06:46.750
No way. We can't fight something like that!

06:46.750 --> 06:49.880
And we just finished getting
this year's budget approved!

06:49.880 --> 06:50.710
No...

06:50.710 --> 06:51.790
It's a joke, right?

06:51.790 --> 06:53.000
Stop saying that.

06:53.420 --> 06:56.500
Now then, before fear and panic
begin to spread among our citizens,

06:56.500 --> 06:58.630
it's our job as the four generals
to handle this situation.

06:58.630 --> 06:59.750
I've got it.

06:59.750 --> 07:01.000
Let's resign.

07:01.000 --> 07:02.000
Hey, wait!

07:02.000 --> 07:04.130
Please don't run away from this, Randan!

07:07.750 --> 07:11.210
<b>Gatekeeper Dragons</b>

07:07.750 --> 07:11.210
<b>Dryme's Lair</b>

07:09.250 --> 07:11.210
Did you see that, Gucci?

07:11.420 --> 07:14.000
I saw it with my own eyes.

07:14.000 --> 07:18.630
And what do you think would happen
if I were to receive such an attack?

07:18.630 --> 07:20.790
It would mostly likely
pierce cleanly through you.

07:22.330 --> 07:23.830
What do we do?

07:23.830 --> 07:25.420
It would be foolish to attack.

07:26.040 --> 07:27.790
Yeah, definitely.

07:35.130 --> 07:38.040
The wyvern meat was every bit
as delicious as it was said to be.

07:38.040 --> 07:42.880
But if I'm being honest, there's still
one thing that was missing from the meal.

07:43.290 --> 07:45.670
Ah, are we going to start now?

07:45.670 --> 07:47.080
Is it finally time?

07:48.580 --> 07:49.540
Yeah.

07:50.830 --> 07:52.540
We're making alcohol!

07:54.540 --> 07:57.790
If we're making alcohol out of grapes,
then it's going to be wine.

07:58.210 --> 08:00.540
Apparently, wine exists in this world.

08:01.080 --> 08:03.830
So, everyone was excited to make it
and quickly harvested all the grapes.

08:03.830 --> 08:07.790
Now all that's left is to squash the grapes
and let them ferment.

08:07.790 --> 08:09.960
and to do that, we built...

08:11.080 --> 08:12.380
this!

08:12.960 --> 08:14.830
We're going to walk on top of these?

08:14.830 --> 08:17.210
Yeah. Make sure to stomp them really good.

08:17.210 --> 08:20.460
I'm a little hesitant to stomp on
something that we're going to drink.

08:20.710 --> 08:23.330
If you get tired, you can have
someone switch in for you.

08:23.330 --> 08:24.710
What about you?

08:24.710 --> 08:28.460
I'm in charge of switching
the barrels as they fill up.

08:28.460 --> 08:32.420
By the way, these barrels were
built by the high elf Lalasha

08:32.420 --> 08:34.080
because she knows how to make
containers that are water tight.

08:33.460 --> 08:34.960
<b>Lalasha</b>

08:34.080 --> 08:34.960
Okay!
because she knows how to make<b>
</b>containers that are water tight.<b></b>

08:35.790 --> 08:37.880
I had her make them right away.

08:38.290 --> 08:40.580
Alright, you guys can start now.

08:43.790 --> 08:46.040
You really sink into them.

08:46.880 --> 08:48.290
Am I doing it right?

08:48.290 --> 08:49.830
Let's see...

08:49.830 --> 08:52.790
Starting moving in a circular motion
around the whole thing.

08:53.330 --> 08:54.420
Okay.

08:55.210 --> 08:57.210
Let's go in this direction.

08:57.210 --> 08:58.170
Yeah.

09:04.170 --> 09:06.040
Careful not to slip and fall.

09:06.710 --> 09:07.790
Okay.

09:14.750 --> 09:16.250
Are you alright?

09:16.250 --> 09:18.250
I-I think so...

09:20.380 --> 09:23.170
I'm sorry that I bumped into you.

09:23.170 --> 09:25.710
Not at all. That was my fault.

09:27.000 --> 09:30.750
You know, I think this would be easier
if we had a way to help keep our rhythm.

09:30.750 --> 09:33.170
One... Two... One... Two...
It might keep all of our movements in sync.<b></b>

09:33.170 --> 09:35.670
Hm, good point.

09:38.040 --> 09:40.920
I know, we can use that song

09:40.920 --> 09:43.880
we used to sing in our village
while we were all working together.

09:43.880 --> 09:45.750
Ah! That just might work!

09:45.750 --> 09:47.420
A song?

09:47.420 --> 09:49.750
Yes. It goes like this.

09:50.750 --> 09:52.880
One, two, three, go!

10:21.460 --> 10:23.290
Looks like they found their rhythm.

10:24.330 --> 10:25.460
Hey, Lu!

10:26.130 --> 10:28.130
Come on, it's fun!

10:28.130 --> 10:30.330
Okay, then you're coming with me!

10:30.330 --> 10:31.540
Huh? But I'm...

10:31.540 --> 10:32.330
Let's go!

10:32.330 --> 10:33.460
Hey, wait!

10:33.460 --> 10:34.460
Come on!

10:34.750 --> 10:35.750
Come on!

10:44.000 --> 10:45.960
That was a lot of work.

10:46.540 --> 10:49.460
I'm exhausted, but that was a lot of fun.

10:50.000 --> 10:54.540
Now the yeast on the skin of the grapes
should ferment this for us.

10:55.790 --> 10:57.710
I wonder if we made too much...

10:56.170 --> 10:57.710
<b>16 barrels total</b>

10:58.040 --> 10:59.500
It'll be fine.

10:59.500 --> 11:02.000
I'm sure we'll drink it all right away.

11:02.000 --> 11:04.670
Yeah, I can't wait to drink it.

11:04.670 --> 11:06.670
Don't tell me we didn't make enough...

11:07.250 --> 11:10.540
See? Look how much fun he's having.

11:10.540 --> 11:13.000
So, can't you forgive me
for what I've done already?

11:13.000 --> 11:14.460
Absolutely not!

11:13.000 --> 11:14.460
<b>Goddess of Agriculture</b>

11:15.040 --> 11:18.420
You mistakenly punished
an innocent human's soul,

11:18.420 --> 11:20.250
and sneakily tried to save him,

11:20.250 --> 11:23.330
only to end up sending him to
that horrible Forest of Death!

11:24.250 --> 11:26.170
On top of that, you gave him that spear!

11:26.170 --> 11:29.040
I can't believe you gave him
a replica of the holy lance Gryme!

11:29.040 --> 11:32.630
Well, um... right now he's only
using it as a farming tool.

11:32.630 --> 11:34.630
Plus, I got permission first, remember?

11:34.630 --> 11:37.210
You didn't tell me you were
giving that to a human!

11:37.210 --> 11:40.960
That thing should drain all of their
life force and kill them instantly!

11:40.960 --> 11:43.500
But he's doing fine right now.

11:43.500 --> 11:46.500
I'm sure that he just has
super-fast recovery abilities

11:46.500 --> 11:49.130
because I gave him such a healthy body...

11:49.130 --> 11:51.420
I'm telling you that you were too careless!

11:51.960 --> 11:53.040
And besides that...

11:53.040 --> 11:54.170
And besides that!

11:56.210 --> 12:00.250
Why is the statue that's
supposed to be me an old man?!

11:59.790 --> 12:01.000
<b>Old man</b>

12:00.710 --> 12:03.040
That's not my fault.

12:03.040 --> 12:04.210
I don't want to hear any excuses!

12:04.210 --> 12:06.880
As punishment, you're going to sit there
like that for 300 years, my careless father!

12:06.880 --> 12:09.920
Please forgive me, my daughter!

12:23.960 --> 12:27.000
I'm feeling a strong sense of déjà vu here.

12:27.000 --> 12:28.080
Flora?!

12:28.080 --> 12:29.380
My dear sister!

12:29.380 --> 12:31.290
So, they're actually related somehow.
My dear sister!<b></b>

12:31.960 --> 12:32.830
Yes!

12:33.170 --> 12:37.920
After I heard you were being chased by
that infamous black-hearted angel,

12:37.920 --> 12:39.580
I followed you all the way here.

12:39.580 --> 12:41.460
Who did you say was black-hearted?

12:41.460 --> 12:43.330
Why is she here?!

12:43.330 --> 12:45.330
It was just an expression!

12:45.330 --> 12:48.710
Apparently, Flora is also a vampire.
It's something I used to hear Lu say very often.<b></b>

12:48.710 --> 12:49.080
Oh, did Lu say that?

12:49.080 --> 12:50.880
And she's related to Lu.
Oh, did Lu say that?<b></b>

12:50.880 --> 12:52.790
Oh sister, please help me!

12:53.130 --> 12:57.290
Well since you're here, why not relax
and stay with us for a while?

12:57.290 --> 12:58.420
Okay...

12:58.960 --> 13:01.790
I'm having a hard time believing that
this man here is Lu's husband.

13:01.790 --> 13:03.710
Something feels off.

13:05.420 --> 13:06.960
No, never mind!

13:07.460 --> 13:09.210
He's the one who's in charge here,

13:09.210 --> 13:11.750
and he's the master of
all these inferno wolves.

13:11.750 --> 13:13.500
He even took down a wyvern.

13:14.170 --> 13:15.750
I understand now.

13:16.250 --> 13:18.040
I humbly apologize for my rude behavior.

13:16.250 --> 13:19.460
<b>Prostrate</b>

13:18.040 --> 13:19.460
Don't worry about it.

13:19.750 --> 13:21.250
So anyways...

13:21.250 --> 13:24.210
You guys are wolves, Kuro?
I had no idea.

13:25.170 --> 13:27.000
What's the inferno part mean?

13:28.830 --> 13:31.000
Wow! That's amazing!

13:32.000 --> 13:34.540
You've been living with them
this whole time and didn't know?

13:34.540 --> 13:37.500
I believe they're quite well-known
magical beasts...

13:41.790 --> 13:43.830
I guess you can think of this
as sort of an apology

13:43.830 --> 13:45.920
for what Kuro and the wolves
put you through.

13:45.920 --> 13:47.790
We went ahead and prepared dinner for you.

13:51.500 --> 13:52.540
It's great!

13:53.330 --> 13:55.170
This is all fantastic.

13:55.170 --> 13:57.540
What's the soft, white stuff?

13:57.540 --> 13:59.420
Oh, that's called tofu.

13:59.420 --> 14:01.880
After a lot of tries, I finally got it right.

14:01.880 --> 14:04.000
They're made from a type of bean
called soybeans.

14:04.000 --> 14:06.540
Wow, this made from beans?

14:06.920 --> 14:10.580
Flavoring soup with salt is fine and all,
but I really wanted some miso.

14:11.000 --> 14:14.080
Plus, I wanted to be able to put
soy sauce on stuff I eat.

14:14.540 --> 14:16.710
Miso? Soy sauce?

14:16.710 --> 14:19.210
Miso and soy sauce are both made
from fermented soybeans

14:19.210 --> 14:20.920
and are used to add flavor to food.

14:20.920 --> 14:22.330
Fermented?!

14:22.500 --> 14:23.710
Basically...

14:23.710 --> 14:29.000
It seems that in this world,
fermented foods like wine and cheese exist.

14:29.830 --> 14:33.460
However, they aren't aware of the microorganisms
that actually cause fermentation.

14:33.460 --> 14:34.960
I see.

14:35.420 --> 14:38.710
If tiny organisms that we aren't
able to see with our eyes exist,

14:38.710 --> 14:42.460
and if these organisms can cause
transformations in matter without magic,

14:42.460 --> 14:45.000
then that would serve to explain all of this.

14:45.000 --> 14:46.130
Eat or talk. Pick one.

14:46.130 --> 14:47.630
It seems that like Lu, she's also
very passionate about her research.
Eat or talk. Pick one.<b></b>

14:47.630 --> 14:49.670
It seems that like Lu, she's also
very passionate about her research.

14:50.330 --> 14:53.460
I've found a fascinating new subject
for my research!

14:54.040 --> 14:57.380
I'll be sure to bring the wonders of miso and
soy sauce to all who live in these lands!

14:57.710 --> 15:02.380
And then one day we will all feast upon
miso soup and cold tofu!

15:03.540 --> 15:05.500
After staying here for a few days,

15:05.500 --> 15:09.000
Flora left with great haste and excitement
so that she could make preparations to move.

15:09.000 --> 15:12.330
<b>1 month later</b>

15:10.500 --> 15:12.330
I have returned!

15:12.500 --> 15:13.500
O-okay...

15:13.500 --> 15:15.380
That was really fast.

15:15.380 --> 15:17.670
You even brought the maids with you.

15:19.670 --> 15:21.130
It's a pleasure to meet you.

15:21.130 --> 15:24.880
My name is Anne, and I speak on behalf of
the other maids as their representative.

15:24.880 --> 15:28.330
We ask that you put us to use
as you see fit, master.

15:28.330 --> 15:31.420
Uh, you really don't need to be that formal.

15:32.170 --> 15:33.750
By the way, what are those?

15:34.380 --> 15:37.540
They're just normal cows, right?

15:37.540 --> 15:39.170
That's right.

15:39.170 --> 15:42.290
I made sure to pick cows to bring
with me that would give us milk.

15:43.790 --> 15:47.380
This is great.
Now we can make butter and cheese!

15:49.670 --> 15:50.250
<b>Vampires and their clan</b>

15:49.670 --> 15:50.250
<b>A lot</b>

15:51.170 --> 15:51.750
<b>Elves</b>

15:51.170 --> 15:51.750
<b>A lot</b>

15:52.670 --> 15:53.250
<b>Wolves</b>

15:52.670 --> 15:53.250
<b>A lot</b>

15:54.170 --> 15:54.750
<b>Spiders</b>

15:54.170 --> 15:54.750
<b>A lot</b>

15:55.670 --> 15:57.630
<b>Angels</b>

15:56.170 --> 15:57.630
<b>by myself</b>

15:56.170 --> 15:57.630
<b>= not many</b>

15:56.170 --> 15:57.630
<b>= WEAK</b>

15:58.000 --> 15:58.920
Excuse me!

15:58.920 --> 16:00.170
What? Why are you so close?

16:00.170 --> 16:02.290
I need to leave for a short while.

16:02.290 --> 16:03.460
Sure...

16:04.380 --> 16:06.790
I wonder what she's going off to do.

16:09.540 --> 16:11.500
<b>Meeting</b>

16:10.880 --> 16:12.670
I have returned!

16:12.960 --> 16:13.960
Okay...

16:13.960 --> 16:16.920
I've brought my underlings here as well!

16:16.920 --> 16:19.040
My name is Granmaria.

16:19.750 --> 16:21.080
I'm Kudel.

16:21.630 --> 16:24.420
I'm Corone. It's nice to meet you.

16:24.750 --> 16:27.630
I'm Daga,
the representative of the lizardmen.

16:27.630 --> 16:30.380
And I've prepared this here as well!

16:30.710 --> 16:32.460
It's a chicken!

16:32.460 --> 16:33.710
Does it breathe fire?

16:33.960 --> 16:34.960
It does not.

16:34.960 --> 16:36.210
What about eggs?

16:36.210 --> 16:37.460
It lays them!

16:37.460 --> 16:38.880
I'm glad to hear it.

16:41.290 --> 16:45.170
Thanks to everyone here,
this place just got a lot more civilized.

16:46.420 --> 16:49.170
For the rooms on this side, Lamulias,

16:49.170 --> 16:51.500
I want you to dust them
before we start washing the floors.

16:51.500 --> 16:52.790
Understood.

16:54.000 --> 16:55.790
Ah, sorry for interrupting.

16:55.790 --> 16:56.790
It's fine.

16:56.790 --> 16:59.880
The maids belong to a race of ogres.

17:00.380 --> 17:02.880
I guess it's to be expected
since they're professionals,

17:02.880 --> 17:06.210
but as soon as they showed up
all of our chores got done a lot faster.

17:06.750 --> 17:07.830
However...

17:08.500 --> 17:12.830
The inhabitants of this world don't seem
to cook any complicated dishes.

17:13.130 --> 17:13.880
<b>Frying</b>

17:13.880 --> 17:14.630
<b>Boiling</b>

17:13.960 --> 17:17.630
I tried to teach them all the different
methods of cooking that I knew.

17:14.630 --> 17:15.380
<b>Stir fry</b>

17:15.380 --> 17:16.130
<b>Deep fry</b>

17:16.130 --> 17:16.880
<b>Braising</b>

17:16.880 --> 17:17.630
<b>Dressing salads</b>

17:17.630 --> 17:18.380
<b>Steaming</b>

17:18.380 --> 17:23.830
<b>Heat control</b>

17:19.920 --> 17:23.830
It seems like it got them
interested in cooking all at once.

17:25.040 --> 17:26.580
Dinner is served.

17:26.580 --> 17:30.130
Today I tried making a dish of
killer rabbit with fragrant vegetables.

17:30.130 --> 17:33.630
Wow. So those things
are called killer rabbits, huh?

17:35.630 --> 17:37.130
This looks wild.

17:37.130 --> 17:40.790
They're all very strong,
despite their appearances.

17:40.790 --> 17:44.920
They display both proper manners
and a bit of power.

17:45.670 --> 17:47.790
Then, there are the three angels
that Tia brought with her.

17:47.790 --> 17:51.420
Now then, you're all to patrol
a different region of the forest.

17:51.420 --> 17:51.880
Granmaria, Kudel, and Corone.

17:51.880 --> 17:54.250
I want you to make sure you see everything,
even the tiniest of movements.
Granmaria, Kudel, and Corone.<b></b>

17:54.250 --> 17:55.250
Understood.
I was wondering why they all showed up<b>
</b>in such serious looking armor.<b></b>

17:55.250 --> 17:57.170
I was wondering why they all showed up
in such serious looking armor.

17:57.540 --> 17:59.830
It turns out that after the wyvern attack,

17:59.830 --> 18:02.460
Tia planned on having them
act as our security on the premises.

18:02.460 --> 18:04.420
I feel safer with them around.

18:04.420 --> 18:05.880
The lizardmen are in charge of all the labor
that requires strength outdoors.

18:05.880 --> 18:06.960
Hey!
The lizardmen are in charge of all the labor<b>
</b>that requires strength outdoors.<b></b>

18:06.960 --> 18:08.290
The lizardmen are in charge of all the labor
that requires strength outdoors.

18:08.290 --> 18:10.170
Yes, I'll be over in just a moment.

18:10.170 --> 18:13.170
Thanks to them, our construction work
is moving along even faster than before.

18:13.670 --> 18:17.880
By the way, I had their leader Daga
tie a scarf around his arm.

18:17.880 --> 18:20.330
I feel bad, but I'm not able to
tell them apart otherwise.

18:20.330 --> 18:21.830
I guess that makes sense.
I feel bad, but I'm not able to<b>
</b>tell them apart otherwise.<b></b>

18:21.830 --> 18:22.790
I guess that makes sense.

18:23.750 --> 18:27.500
Now that I think about it, this place
is really filling up with people living here.

18:28.210 --> 18:30.960
<b>Population</b>

18:28.330 --> 18:29.960
How many of us are there now?

18:32.380 --> 18:33.380
A lot.

18:33.380 --> 18:34.380
Hiraku!

18:35.380 --> 18:38.040
I brought all the elves that were still
wandering the forest over here!

18:38.040 --> 18:39.290
Oh...

18:41.380 --> 18:43.210
N-now there are even more...

18:43.210 --> 18:44.670
Are they all women?

18:44.670 --> 18:46.960
Where are the men? I don't see any.

18:47.330 --> 18:50.170
There weren't really any men who survived.

18:50.170 --> 18:51.500
I see.

18:52.040 --> 18:53.880
But that's okay.

18:54.170 --> 18:56.540
We can just start making more now!

18:58.080 --> 18:59.790
I hope that works out for you!

18:59.790 --> 19:02.250
I decided not to ask them
how they planned to do it.

19:02.830 --> 19:05.290
<b>A few days later</b>

19:04.710 --> 19:06.790
Hey, what's going on?

19:06.790 --> 19:10.040
Who knows? I'm just here
because I was asked to come.

19:10.040 --> 19:13.500
He said to gather all the different
representatives here today...

19:13.500 --> 19:16.500
I wonder if some sort of problem has arisen.

19:16.750 --> 19:21.500
Hey, sorry for calling you all here like this.

19:22.540 --> 19:24.880
There's something I want to talk about
with all of you today.

19:26.210 --> 19:29.500
You see, I want to come up with
a name for this place.

19:29.500 --> 19:32.080
This place here?

19:32.080 --> 19:33.000
Yeah.

19:33.500 --> 19:36.500
At first, it was just my little hut
and some crop fields,

19:36.500 --> 19:40.170
but then more buildings started popping up
and more people started moving in.

19:40.170 --> 19:42.130
It's like a village now, right?

19:42.580 --> 19:46.000
That's why I want to come up with
a name for this village.

19:46.000 --> 19:47.460
I like that idea!

19:47.460 --> 19:49.750
A name for our town!

19:50.000 --> 19:53.830
Can't we just name it after you
since you're the founder?

19:53.830 --> 19:54.790
No...

19:54.790 --> 20:00.250
<b>Welcome</b>

19:54.790 --> 19:56.670
<b>Come to Hiraku Village</b>

19:55.210 --> 19:57.170
Then it'd be something like Hiraku Village,

19:56.670 --> 20:00.250
<b>Gather at Machio Town</b>

19:57.170 --> 19:58.710
or maybe Machio Town.

19:58.710 --> 20:00.250
I don't really like the sound of that.

20:00.630 --> 20:04.250
In that case, how about we name it
after the forest we're in?

20:04.250 --> 20:06.170
That sounds like a good idea.

20:06.170 --> 20:08.670
By the way, what's this forest called?

20:08.670 --> 20:10.290
The Forest of Death.

20:08.670 --> 20:11.880
<b>The Forest of Death</b>

20:10.290 --> 20:11.580
What, really? That's scary.

20:11.580 --> 20:13.500
That makes this The Village of Death.

20:11.920 --> 20:16.630
<b>The Village of Death</b>

20:13.500 --> 20:14.750
Sounds like a ghost town.

20:14.750 --> 20:16.630
It sounds like it'd have a poison swamp.

20:18.670 --> 20:19.880
What is it?

20:21.790 --> 20:23.380
This door?

20:24.330 --> 20:25.920
You want me to open it?

20:32.460 --> 20:34.210
This is The Great Tree Village.

20:45.960 --> 20:47.960
Hello, everyone.

20:47.960 --> 20:52.000
From now on, we've decided to
call this The Great Tree Village.

20:52.580 --> 20:54.830
In celebration of this day,

20:54.830 --> 20:56.420
we're going to have a party!

20:58.000 --> 21:00.330
And no party would be complete without this!

21:00.330 --> 21:03.750
The first batch of wine we made
here in The Great Tree Village!

21:05.040 --> 21:07.460
Please enjoy yourselves, everyone!

21:09.500 --> 21:11.000
Mayor!

21:11.750 --> 21:12.960
Mayor!

21:15.960 --> 21:19.040
Mayor! Mayor!
No, that's something we need to<b>
</b>decide together later.<b></b>

21:19.040 --> 21:20.710
What are you talking about?

21:20.710 --> 21:22.830
You're the only one for the job.

21:23.130 --> 21:26.130
She's right.
Everyone's already calling you mayor!

21:28.040 --> 21:30.040
I-I see.

21:59.460 --> 22:01.250
<b>Fermentation</b>

22:25.290 --> 22:26.790
You're pretty drunk, huh?

22:27.210 --> 22:30.790
What's wrong?
You're sitting all by yourself zoning out.

22:31.210 --> 22:32.540
It's nothing.

22:33.210 --> 22:39.250
I was just thinking about how I'm so happy
that this all feels like a dream.

22:40.960 --> 22:42.880
This isn't a dream.

22:42.880 --> 22:46.580
We're all going to keep living together,
enjoying our lives.

22:47.790 --> 22:49.420
Yeah, you're right.

22:49.420 --> 22:51.040
I'd like that.

22:51.040 --> 22:52.330
Okay then!

22:54.210 --> 22:56.830
Let's toast to The Great Tree Village.

22:58.630 --> 22:59.670
Yeah.

23:00.420 --> 23:01.630
Cheers.

23:04.080 --> 23:05.540
No fair!

23:05.750 --> 23:08.710
I'm going to toast, too!

23:09.380 --> 23:11.460
You were awake?

23:11.710 --> 23:13.040
C'mon!

23:13.040 --> 23:15.330
Very well then.

23:16.710 --> 23:18.540
How many years has it been?

23:18.540 --> 23:19.630
Cheers!

23:19.630 --> 23:23.170
It's been a while since I've had wine.
It tastes better than I remember.

23:23.170 --> 23:24.290
Gimme another!

23:38.080 --> 23:40.460
I guess I'll give it a shot,

23:40.460 --> 23:41.710
as mayor.

23:46.080 --> 23:47.500
<b>Next Time</b>

23:47.500 --> 23:51.000
<b>Episode 7</b>

23:47.500 --> 23:51.000
<b>A Hospitable Heart</b>

23:47.500 --> 23:51.000
<b>Next Time</b>
